meta {
  name: upload file
  type: http
  seq: 51
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/administrator/upload/
  body: multipartForm
  auth: inherit
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file()
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  Uploads one file and returns a public URL. Nothing is stored on this server --
  the file is forwarded to Ongshak's transfer service and only the resulting URL
  is kept, which is why every model field is a `*_url` rather than a `FileField`.

  Pick the file in Bruno's UI for the `file` field (it is the only field, and it
  is required).

  Rules enforced by the view:

  - Maximum 20 MB; anything larger returns 400.
  - A `.jpg`, `.jpeg` or `.png` over 2 MB is compressed at level 50 on the way through.
  - Files land under the `vida_verde` path (`TRANSFER_ONGSHAK_PATH`).

  Requires `TRANSFER_ONGSHAK_API_KEY` in `server/.env` -- still to be supplied.

  Use the returned URL for `profile_img_url`, `image_url`, `photo_url` or an
  entry in a blog's `image_urls`.

  ## API example response
  {
    "success": true,
    "url": "https://transfer2.ongshak.com/vida_verde/fernando-cordero.jpg",
    "filename": "fernando-cordero.jpg",
    "size": 184320
  }
}
